    a parent directory's `.packignore` come before rules from a child
    directory's file. If no rule matches, the path takes its parent
    directory's state. Files that are executable (any execute bit set) or
    whose first line contains `@generated` are excluded by default. Any rule
    that matches the file itself overrides that default.
    A `.packignore` inside an excluded directory is not read.

Only regular files are considered. Symlinks are skipped and so are symlinked
directories. A `.git` directory directly under the root is skipped too.
